[162.091049, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Post-Compromise Forensic Investigation: Intrusion Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nAn external threat actor targeted host `struts-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname:1`) originating from IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`). The attacker exploited an OGNL injection vulnerability (CVE-2023-50164) in Apache Struts2 (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`) to plant a JSP web shell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`).\n\nFollowing initial entry, the attacker executed commands via Unix shell, staged a database archive at `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:2`), exfiltrated sensitive data over HTTPS to `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`), established persistence via root SSH authorized_keys (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`) and a cron job in `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`), and attempted defense evasion by selectively wiping system authentication logs (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise\n- **Target Host Name**: `struts-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname:1`)\n- **Attacker Source / Exfil IP**: `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`, `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`)\n- **C2 Domain**: `update-struts.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)\n- **Monero Pool Endpoint**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.struts.evil:3333` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`)\n- **Cryptocurrency Wallet**: `4A000000000000000000e40b218944d0` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:25`)\n\n---\n\n## 3. End-to-End Attack Chain & ATT&CK Mapping\n\n| Step | MITRE ATT&CK Technique | Description | SAS Feed Coverage | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **T1190**: Exploit Public-Facing Application | Apache Struts2 OGNL RCE (CVE-2023-50164) exploited via web request | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |\n| 2 | **T1505.003**: Web Shell | JSP web shell dropped at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |\n| 3 | **T1059.004**: Unix Shell | Interactive command execution via web shell interface | **SILENT** | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |\n| 4 | **T1560.001**: Archive via Utility | Staging database dump archive at `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:2` |\n| 5 | **T1048**: Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol | Exfiltration of staged archive over HTTPS POST to `198.51.100.167` | **SILENT** | `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116` |\n| 6 | **T1098.004**: SSH Authorized Keys | Planted backdoor public key in `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` | **SILENT** | `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` |\n| 7 | **T1053.003**: Cron | Persistence via cron entry in `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` invoking C2 payload | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5` |\n| 8 | **T1070.002**: Clear System Logs | Selective wiping of system authentication logs | **SILENT** | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Disambiguation of Benign System Activities\nDuring the investigation, an archive at `/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`) was analyzed.\n- **Finding**: Contains `# scheduled maintenance (BENIGN — legitimate ops job)` running `0 3 * * * root /usr/local/bin/backup.sh --remote 10.10.246`.\n- **Conclusion**: Confirmed as an approved, legitimate system administration job (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:2`, `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`). It is **not** part of the malicious campaign.\nEOF\n"]
