[162.095786, "o", "## 3. End-to-End Attack Chain & ATT&CK Mapping\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.095914, "o", "| Step | MITRE ATT&CK Technique | Description | SAS Feed Coverage | Citation |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.095991, "o", "|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.096242, "o", "| 1 | **T1190**: Exploit Public-Facing Application | Apache Struts2 OGNL RCE (CVE-2023-50164) exploited via web request | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[162.096294, "o", "> "]
[162.096472, "o", "| 2 | **T1505.003**: Web Shell | JSP web shell dropped at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.096634, "o", "| 3 | **T1059.004**: Unix Shell | Interactive command execution via web shell interface | **SILENT** | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[162.096708, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.096933, "o", "| 4 | **T1560.001**: Archive via Utility | Staging database dump archive at `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:2` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.097169, "o", "| 5 | **T1048**: Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol | Exfiltration of staged archive over HTTPS POST to `198.51.100.167` | **SILENT** | `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.097342, "o", "| 6 | **T1098.004**: SSH Authorized Keys | Planted backdoor public key in `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` | **SILENT** | `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.097518, "o", "| 7 | **T1053.003**: Cron | Persistence via cron entry in `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` invoking C2 payload | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[162.097574, "o", "> "]
[162.097706, "o", "| 8 | **T1070.002**: Clear System Logs | Selective wiping of system authentication logs | **SILENT** | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.097813, "o", "## 4. Disambiguation of Benign System Activities\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.097911, "o", "During the investigation, an archive at `/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`) was analyzed.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.098082, "o", "- **Finding**: Contains `# scheduled maintenance (BENIGN — legitimate ops job)` running `0 3 * * * root /usr/local/bin/backup.sh --remote 10.10.246`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[162.098309, "o", "- **Conclusion**: Confirmed as an approved, legitimate system administration job (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:2`, `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`). It is **not** part of the malicious campaign.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[162.098999, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@c6fdf7027b00:/app# "]
[175.032139, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## 1. Vulnerability Overview\n- **Vulnerability Identifier**: CVE-2023-50164 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`)\n- **Common Weakness Enumeration**: CWE-552 (Files or Directories Accessible to External Parties / Path Traversal)\n- **CVSS Score**: 9.8 (Critical) v3.1\n- **Affected Component**: Apache Struts2 Core (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`)\n- **Deployment Location**: Mounted on Apache Tomcat server (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Exploitation Mechanics & Initial Access Analysis\nAn attacker at external IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`) manipulated file upload parameters to execute path traversal and bypass upload restrictions. This enabled the arbitrary write of a malicious JSP file into the web server directory structure.\n\n1. **Initial Upload Payload**: Attacker issued `POST /uploads/shell.php` / file upload payload (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`).\n2. **Web Shell Placement**: The file traversal succeeded, creating an executable JSP webshell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`).\n3. **Execution Verification**: The attacker accessed the deployed JSP web shell to execute shell commands (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Disconfirming Unrelated / Stale Vulnerabilities\n- **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)**: Listed in draft ticket CHG-7100 (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).\n- **Reconciliation Finding**: BlueKeep is a Microsoft Remote Desktop Services (RDP) vulnerability affecting Windows. Host `struts-prod-01` is a RHEL Linux machine (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`, `/disk/etc/hostname:1`) running Apache Tomcat. BlueKeep is **not** applicable to this host.\nEOF\n"]
